  "notes": "UGLY TRUTH — the emotional gut-punch. The axes dramatically extend downward and rightward, revealing vast empty space where the non-OECD countries will appear. This visual alone tells the story before any dot appears. 6 non-OECD dots use SQUARES (not circles) to visually distinguish them from OECD data and reinforce the disclaimer that these use different data sources. They appear sequentially with fade-drop animation. The OECD cluster suddenly looks tiny and privileged. DEU-KHM connector stretches across nearly the entire chart — the most dramatic visual in the video. Script mentions Germany earns the entire Bangladeshi annual salary in ~5 weeks. Disclaimer text persists in corner. Math verified: DEU $51.82/hr / KHM $2.30/hr = 22.53× ≈ 22.5×. LUX $64.12/hr / IND $3.61/hr = 17.76× ≈ 17.8×. PAK 2,471 hrs is most in entire 40-country dataset. MEX $9.18 vs KHM $2.30 — even OECD worst is 4× better than non-OECD worst."
